	(text "# MCU SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (MCU BLOCK)\n\nProject: OpenMycoNet COMBO_NODE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 3.6\n\n---\n\n### SYSTEM OVERVIEW\n\nThe MCU subsystem centers on the ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 module (U6) operating from a regulated +3.3V digital supply rail. It controls real-time sensor sampling, dual-mode analog front-end multiplexing, SPI/I2C communication, power gating load switches, and external window watchdog supervision.\n\n---\n\n### 1. SYSTEM CORE AND POWER\n\n* Core Module: U6 (ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8).\n* Power Rail Filtering: Parallel ceramic decoupling capacitors connected directly across +3.3V (Pin 2) to GND (Pin 1).\n* Hardware Reset: Active-LOW ~RESET line on EN (Pin 3) pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R27 (10kΩ) and debounced by C18 (100nF) via SW1 push button. Driven by watchdog supervisor U7 output (~RESET).\n* Hardware Watchdog Supervisor: U7 (TPS3851H33EDDAR) monitors system software execution via RST_WDI (IO4 / Pin 4). If no heartbeat pulse is toggled within the 323.4 ms window (C45 = 100nF), U7 asserts ~RESET_CHIP LOW to perform a hard chip reset.\n* Sleep Mode Watchdog Disable: WCD_SLEEP (IO47 / Pin 24) drives U7 SET1 (Pin 5). Driving IO47 LOW before entering deep sleep cleanly disables the watchdog supervisor.\n\n---\n\n### 2. BOOT, STRAPPING AND MEMORY CONFIGURATION\n\n* Bootloader Download Mode: IO0 (Pin 27) connected to BOOT0 net, pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R28 (10kΩ) and grounded via SW2 push button (debounced by C19 = 100nF).\n* ROM Log Suppression Strapping: IO45 (Pin 26) and IO46 (Pin 16) pulled LOW to GND via R24 (10kΩ) and R25 (10kΩ) respectively to suppress internal ROM boot debug messages.\n* Octal PSRAM Protection: IO35 (Pin 28), IO36 (Pin 29), and IO37 (Pin 30) explicitly unassigned (NC) to avoid memory bus conflicts with internal Octal PSRAM routing.\n\n---\n\n### 3. BUS PULL-UPS AND CONTROL LOGIC\n\n* Battery Interrupt: IO21 (Pin 23) receives active-LOW BATT_ALERT signal from fuel gauge, pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R20 (10kΩ).\n* Shared I2C Bus Pull-Ups: I2C_BUS.SCL (IO8 / Pin 12) and I2C_BUS.SDA (IO9 / Pin 17) pulled HIGH to +3.3V via resistors R17 (4.7kΩ) and R18 (4.7kΩ).\n* Analog Front-End Shutdown Control: IO42 (Pin 35) outputs ANA_SHUT net to control OPA2320S shutdown pins (~SHDN1/~SHDN2), pulled LOW to GND via R23 (10kΩ).\n* Dual-Mode Analog Switch Control: IO48 (Pin 25) outputs EC_ENABLE net to toggle TS5A3159 analog switch path, pulled LOW to GND via R26 (10kΩ).\n* Soil Moisture Power Control: IO41 (Pin 34) outputs MOISTURE_SLEEP net to drive U18 (TPS22919) load switch, gating power to off-board moisture probes.\n* MicroSD Power Control: IO40 (Pin 33) outputs SD_CARD_SLEEP net to drive U17 (TPS22919) load switch.\n* ADC Interrupt Pull-Ups: IO38 (Pin 31, ALERT_RDY_ALERT_1) and IO39 (Pin 32, ALERT_RDY_ALERT_2) pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R21 (10kΩ) and R22 (10kΩ) to support open-drain ADS1115 interrupt outputs.\n\n---\n\n### 4. MASTER GPIO ASSIGNMENT TABLE (REV 3.5 EXACT SCHEMATIC MATCH)\n\n| PIN# | GPIO / PIN NAME | NET NAME / SIGNAL | FUNCTION & CONFIGURATION DESCRIPTION |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | GND | GND | System ground reference connection |\n| 2 | 3V3 | +3.3V | Main +3.3V system power supply rail |\n| 3 | EN | RESET_CHIP | System hardware reset line (Pulled HIGH via R27, connected to U7 ~RESET) |\n| 27 | IO0 | BOOT0 | Bootloader download mode select (Pulled HIGH via R28, debounced by SW2/C19) |\n| 39 | IO1 | SPI.SPI_NSS | LoRa Transceiver Chip Select line |\n| 38 | IO2 | DAC_OUT | 16 Hz AC excitation output line for bio-potential sensor |\n| 15 | IO3 | NC | Isolated strapping pin (Pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R19 10kΩ) |\n| 4 | IO4 | RST_WDI | TPS3851H33 Watchdog WDI input pulse line (Toggled during execution) |\n| 5 | IO5 | RTC_IN | DS3231MZ real-time clock alarm interrupt input |\n| 6 | IO6 | DS18B20_DATA | DS18B20 1-wire temperature sensor data bus (Pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R61 4.7kΩ)  |\n| 7 | IO7 | RESET_LoRa | Active-LOW hardware reset line for SX1262 LoRa transceiver |\n| 12 | IO8 | I2C_BUS.SCL | Shared I2C bus clock line (Pulled HIGH via R17 4.7kΩ) |\n| 17 | IO9 | I2C_BUS.SDA | Shared I2C bus data line (Pulled HIGH via R18 4.7kΩ) |\n| 18 | IO10 | BUSY_LoRa | SX1262 LoRa internal status indicator line |\n| 19 | IO11 | DIO1 | SX1262 LoRa interrupt request line |\n| 20 | IO12 | SPI.SPI_MISO | Shared SPI bus Master-In Slave-Out data line |\n| 21 | IO13 | SPI.SPI_MOSI | Shared SPI bus Master-Out Slave-In data line |\n| 22 | IO14 | SPI.SPI_SCK | Shared SPI bus serial clock line |\n| 8 | IO15 | SPI.SPI_CS | Active-LOW MicroSD chip select line |\n| 9 | IO16 | SPI.SD_DET | MicroSD card detect input line |\n| 10 | IO17 | LED_PWM2 | PWM gate drive for LED MOSFET driver Q2 |\n| 11 | IO18 | LED_PWM1 | PWM gate drive for LED MOSFET driver Q1 |\n| 13 | USB_D- | USB_DATA.USB_D- | Native USB 2.0 full-speed data minus line |\n| 14 | USB_D+ | USB_DATA.USB_D+ | Native USB 2.0 full-speed data plus line |\n| 23 | IO21 | BATT_ALERT | Active-LOW fuel gauge state-of-charge interrupt (Pulled HIGH via R20) |\n| 28 | IO35 | NC | Reserved for internal Octal PSRAM (Unconnected / No Connect) |\n| 29 | IO36 | NC | Reserved for internal Octal PSRAM (Unconnected / No Connect) |\n| 30 | IO37 | NC | Reserved for internal Octal PSRAM (Unconnected / No Connect) |\n| 31 | IO38 | ALERT_RDY.ALERT_1 | ADS1115 #1 hardware interrupt/wake-up line (Pulled HIGH via R21) |\n| 32 | IO39 | ALERT_RDY.ALERT_2 | ADS1115 #2 hardware interrupt/wake-up line (Pulled HIGH via R22) |\n| 33 | IO40 | SD_CARD_SLEEP | High-side load switch enable for MicroSD (U17) |\n| 34 | IO41 | MOISTURE_SLEEP | High-side load switch enable for Soil Moisture (U18) |\n| 35 | IO42 | ANA_SHUT | Analog front-end shutdown control line (Pulled LOW via R23 10kΩ) |\n| 26 | IO45 | GND (Strapping) | Boot strapping pin (Pulled LOW to GND via R24 10kΩ) |\n| 16 | IO46 | GND (Strapping) | Boot strapping pin (Pulled LOW to GND via R25 10kΩ) |\n| 24 | IO47 | WCD_SLEEP | Watchdog enable control line (U7 SET1 pin, Pulled LOW via R55 100kΩ) |\n| 25 | IO48 | EC_ENABLE | Digital control line for analog switch (Pulled LOW via R26 10kΩ) |\n| 37 | TXD0 | UART_TX | Debug hardware UART0 transmit line |\n| 36 | RXD0 | UART_RX | Debug hardware UART0 receive line |\n\n---\n\n### 5. EXPANSION HEADER J3 INTERFACE\n\n* Pin 1: I2C_BUS.SCL (Shared I2C clock line from IO8 / Pin 12)\n* Pin 2: I2C_BUS.SDA (Shared I2C data line from IO9 / Pin 17)\n* Pin 3: SPI.SPI_MOSI (Shared SPI Master-Out Slave-In from IO13 / Pin 21)\n* Pin 4: SPI.SPI_SCK (Shared SPI clock from IO14 / Pin 22)\n* Pin 5: SPI.SPI_MISO (Shared SPI Master-In Slave-Out from IO12 / Pin 20)\n* Pin 6: GND (Ground reference connection)\n* Pin 7: +3.3V (Digital system 3.3V supply)\n* Pin 8: UART_RX (Hardware UART0 receive on RXD0 / Pin 36)\n* Pin 9: +3.3V (Digital system 3.3V supply)\n* Pin 10: UART_TX (Hardware UART0 transmit on TXD0 / Pin 37)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
